# The Tsolenka Pass: the notice at the gate (prop) and the roc's shadow (random event on the mountain roads).

~ gate
if flag.tsolenka_gate_open
Narrator: The old notice still hangs by the gate, its warning addressed to nobody. Behind it, the portcullis stands up in its slot, and the road goes on into the cloud.
-> END
endif
Narrator: A board is nailed up beside the portcullis, its letters cut deep and filled with lead so the weather couldn't take them: BY ORDER OF THE CROWN. THE ROAD ABOVE IS CLOSED. NOTHING COMES DOWN. NO ONE GOES UP. APPLY TO THE WATCH.
if not flag.tsolenka_watch_met
quest the_tsolenka_gate reached
endif
interject tag:curious: "Nothing comes down." Not "no one". Nothing.
interject class:wizard: The portcullis is iron a hand thick, and it's warded. Nobody's lifting that from out here. The winch will be inside the tower.
* Look for a way into the tower. -> gate_tower
* Leave it. -> END

~ gate_tower
Narrator: A low door in the tower's side, left of the gate, stands closed but not barred. A thin grey light shows under it, the colour of a lantern seen through fog.
-> END

~ roc_shadow
set roc_seen
cutscene roc_shadow
Narrator: The light goes, all at once, as if a lid has been put on the valley. Then it comes back. High above the road something the size of a ship's sail banks over the ridge, turns its head to look down at you, and decides you are too small to bother with. Today.
cutscene roc_looks_down
interject tag:blunt: Count the wingspan. Then don't.
interject class:wizard: A roc. They nest on high crags and take cattle the way an owl takes mice. The Tsolenka Pass is said to have one.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The curtain of green fire (props tsolenka_green_fire_w and _e)

# The book hangs a curtain of green fire behind the gate and says it can be crossed or dispelled (Elven Tower, Curse of
# Strahd chapter 9); it gives no numbers. The rest is ours: the curtain stands once the portcullis is up, an
# Arcana try (one for the whole party: a failure closes it) or Dispel Magic puts it out for good, and walking into it is
# the trap tsolenka_green_fire (tsolenka_pass.json, 4d10 fire, Dexterity 15 for half, spent when it goes off). Every
# way works for any party; nothing here depends on a social check.

~ green_fire
Narrator: Behind the iron teeth hangs a sheet of green flame, standing upright across the arch like a drawn curtain. It hums in your teeth and throws a sick, pale light over the stone.
Narrator: Hold your hand near and your skin prickles with cold, as if the fire is taking heat instead of giving it.
-> green_fire_menu

~ green_fire_menu
* [if not flag.tsolenka_fire_unpick_tried] [Arcana DC 15] Study the weave for the knot that holds it. -> green_fire_unpicked | green_fire_tangled
* [knows:dispel_magic] (Cast Dispel Magic on the curtain.) -> green_fire_dispelled
* Step back from it. -> END

~ green_fire_unpicked
set tsolenka_green_fire_out
Narrator: Every spell has a seam if you know where to look. One thread pulled loose and the green curtain folds in on itself, vanishing with a dry click.
-> END

~ green_fire_tangled
set tsolenka_fire_unpick_tried
Narrator: You trace the green weave for a loose thread, but the flame only flares higher, humming like a wasp in a jar.
-> green_fire_menu

~ green_fire_dispelled
set tsolenka_green_fire_out
Narrator: You speak the word that unmakes work, and the green curtain shrinks to a cold spark the size of a pin, then goes out without smoke.
-> END
